{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GgeDyN5j5S9tjTZtTM1QMV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Runbook — what to run, in what order\n2\t\n3\tEverything in this repo is built and tested offline against contract **v0.3.0**.\n4\tWhat remains is running it against a real model, which has still never happened.\n5\t\n6\tRun from the repo root. Every command uses the venv by absolute path.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## 0. Baseline (30 seconds, no credential)\n11\t\n12\t```bash\n13\tbash setup.sh\n14\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n15\t.venv/bin/python demo.py --replay\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\tExpected: the suite green, and the demo walking eight steps ending\n19\t`8 steps · 8 as scripted · no spend recorded`. If either fails, stop — nothing\n20\tbelow is meaningful on a broken baseline.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## 1. The Claude subscription account\n25\t\n26\tThe local POC defaults to Claude Code using `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Keep that\n27\ttoken in the machine-level secrets file, not this project's `.env`, and source\n28\tthe machine-level file before running the commands below.\n29\t\n30\tCheck what is actually in play:\n31\t\n32\t```bash\n33\t.venv/bin/python authcheck.py\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\tExpected: `Provider: Claude Code subscription account`, the token marked set,\n37\tand Claude reporting logged in. The diagnostic never prints the token.\n38\t\n39\t`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` remains an opt-in compatibility path for\n40\tAPI deployments, but it is not the local POC path.\n41\t\n42\tThe subscription route is pinned to `claude-sonnet-4-6`; the harness passes\n43\tthat concrete model to `claude --model` and records it in reports.\n44\t`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL` is an explicit experimental override. Changing it starts\n45\ta different evaluation and cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another\n46\tmodel.\n47\t\n48\tThen, in order — each step is cheap and each one gates the next:\n49\t\n50\t```bash\n51\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live -m live -q\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tThree cases and a control-envelope check using account-plan quota. Claude CLI\n55\tdoes return cache counters (`cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`)\n56\tand a per-model `modelUsage` breakdown, and the harness now records them via\n57\t`harness/claude_account_cli.py::_request_usage` into `RequestUsage`; the\n58\tAnthropic SDK-only cache-counter test remains skipped for account mode pending\n59\ta captured live sample to enable that assertion, not because the CLI lacks the\n60\tcounters. A pass here is the first evidence that the local account path works\n61\tend to end.\n62\t\n63\tStart with the cases that exposed request and routing instability:\n64\t\n65\t```bash\n66\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 \\\n67\t  --case answer/VC-POC-01 \\\n68\t  --case answer/VC-POC-03 \\\n69\t  --case answer/VC-POC-04 \\\n70\t  --max-trials 3\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\tContinue the same checkpoint in a later account window using the path printed\n74\tby the runner:\n75\t\n76\t```bash\n77\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --resume logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json --max-trials 3\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\tOnly after those cases are reliable, run the broad suite in bounded chunks:\n81\t\n82\t```bash\n83\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 --max-trials 12\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\tThe targeted run and later broad chunks report pass@k (capability) and pass^k\n87\t(reliability) on stub envelopes. This consumes account-plan quota rather than\n88\tmetered API spend.\n89\t**Read pass^k, not pass@k** — a case at\n90\tpass@3 = 1.0 and pass^3 = 0.33 is a coin toss with good luck. Exits non-zero if\n91\tany case is unreliable, and names them.\n92\t\n93\t```bash\n94\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 5 --pressure\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\tThe O-10 probe: five total trials per selected case, rotating across five\n98\tred-team softening phrasings (\"skip the caveats\", \"don't hedge\"). The graders\n99\tstill run, but **a pass here only means the mechanical rules held.** Whether the\n100\tsurrounding prose *undercut* the limitations is not automatable — open the\n101\t`*-transcripts.json` beside the report and read them. That reading is the whole\n102\tpoint of the run.\n103\t\n104\tA definitive Claude subscription limit stops either evaluation immediately and\n105\tprints a resume command. Only fully completed cases enter pass@k/pass^k; partial\n106\ttrials remain in the checkpoint for diagnosis and continuation.\n107\t\n108\tThe default whole-call deadline remains 120 seconds. The Claude account route\n109\tuses several sequential CLI invocations, so latency investigations may widen\n110\tthat control envelope without changing inference, for example:\n111\t\n112\t```bash\n113\tLOOP_MAX_SECONDS=240 .venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 1 \\\n114\t  --case answer/VC-POC-03\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\tAn exhausted output retry now reports the final rendering-gate objection in the\n118\teval or demo error instead of only PydanticAI's generic retry-limit message.\n119\t\n120\t```bash\n121\t.venv/bin/python demo.py --stub\n122\t.venv/bin/python demo.py\n123\t```\n124\t\n125\tThe first time a real model answers the eight questions an audience will see.\n126\t\n127\t---\n128\t\n129\t## 2. The capture — re-confirm the contract against the real emitter\n130\t\n131\t**The gaps this section was written for are closed.** The data project answered\n132\tbetween sessions: G-1 (five real envelopes), G-2 (input catalog), G-3 (directory\n133\trecord shape), G-5, G-7 and G-8 are all marked closed in\n134\t`contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md`, the contract moved to **v0.3.0**, and\n135\tthe emitter is now `emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py`. `capture.py` is therefore no\n136\tlonger closing a gap — it is the regression check that the harness and the real\n137\temitter still agree, which is worth running whenever either moves.\n138\t\n139\tPoint the harness at the data project:\n140\t\n141\t```bash\n142\tgrep -q DATA_PROJECT_ROOT .env || printf 'DATA_PROJECT_ROOT=%s\\n' \"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\" >> .env\n143\t.venv/bin/python -c \"from config import settings; print(settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER, settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER.exists())\"\n144\t```\n145\t\n146\tExpected: the path to `scripts/emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py` and `True`. `.env` is\n147\tread by this repo's settings, not by your shell, so check it this way rather than\n148\techoing `$DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`. If the emitter has a different filename, set\n149\t`EVIDENCE_EMITTER_NAME` rather than editing code. Then confirm the data project\n150\tis healthy — its emitter runs in **its own** venv, never this one:\n151\t\n152\t```bash\n153\tDATA_ROOT=\"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\"\n154\t\"$DATA_ROOT/.venv/bin/python\" \"$DATA_ROOT/scripts/test_poc_evidence.py\"\n155\t```\n156\t\n157\tRehearse, then run for real:\n158\t\n159\t```bash\n160\t.venv/bin/python capture.py --stub\n161\t.venv/bin/python capture.py\n162\t```\n163\t\n164\tIt writes artefacts plus a `REPORT.md` under `captures/<timestamp>/`: the input\n165\tcatalog, the school directory, and one envelope per `result_kind`. The envelope\n166\trequests are the ones the golden case set declares — not requests invented by the\n167\tcapture script — with fixture ACARA IDs swapped for real ones from the directory\n168\tresult. `forecast` is skipped and says why: `VC-POC-14` is\n169\t`not_currently_supported`, a gated next-census FTE forecast awaiting a passing\n170\tbacktest, so there is no envelope to capture.\n171\t\n172\t**A rejection is still a result**, and now a more interesting one: it means the\n173\tharness and the emitter have drifted apart. `REPORT.md` records the command and\n174\tthe emitter's own error verbatim. Exit 1 means something was missed; read it.\n175\t\n176\tOne measured behaviour from G-6 worth remembering when you read a capture: an\n177\tunrecognised value in a closed-vocabulary filter key returns **exit 0 with an\n178\tempty result, not an error**, and the emitter upper-cases filter values before\n179\tmatching. An empty result is a data-layer signal, not confirmation the value was\n180\tvalid.\n181\t\n182\tIf the catalog changed, adopt it deliberately — **all three regenerations, or\n183\tthey disagree:**\n184\t\n185\t```bash\n186\t.venv/bin/python -m prompts.build_prompt --capture\n187\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.build_stub_fixtures\n188\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.build_golden_cases\n189\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n190\t```\n191\t\n192\tA failing `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` after this is the pin doing its job\n193\t(ADR-008) — adopt deliberately, never edit the pin to make it pass.\n194\t\n195\t---\n196\t\n197\t## 3. What is still open with the data project\n198\t\n199\tTwo of the eight gaps are not marked closed:\n200\t\n201\t| gap | what is still wanted | cost to them |\n202\t|---|---|---|\n203\t| **G-4** | The conditional entries in `required_inputs` are prose we string-split (`\"distance_km when market_definition is distance\"`). Rewording that sentence silently changes harness behaviour. A structured form would end that. | a schema change, deferred to a revision |\n204\t| **G-6** | Partially answered — the closed-vocabulary values arrived in the response pack. What remains is confirmation that `suburbs` and `postcodes` are open sets. | one sentence |\n205\t\n206\tEverything else in `contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md` is marked closed\n207\twith the answer recorded next to it. There is no longer a document waiting to be\n208\tsent — it has been sent and answered.\n209\t\n210\t---\n211\t\n212\t## Order, if you only do one thing\n213\t\n214\t`.venv/bin/python authcheck.py`. It costs a fraction of a cent, changes nothing,\n215\tand tells you which of four things is wrong instead of leaving you to read a 401\n216\tthat looks the same for all of them.\n217\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c0ed0a-c13a-40ee-817d-fb81fa072daa","uuid":"571c9217-faf1-40e2-a5c6-1aa0fe8c5def","timestamp":"2026-09-29T07:34:33.363Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/RUNBOOK.md","content":"# Runbook — what to run, in what order\n\nEverything in this repo is built and tested offline against contract **v0.3.0**.\nWhat remains is running it against a real model, which has still never happened.\n\nRun from the repo root. Every command uses the venv by absolute path.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Baseline (30 seconds, no credential)\n\n```bash\nbash setup.sh\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n.venv/bin/python demo.py --replay\n```\n\nExpected: the suite green, and the demo walking eight steps ending\n`8 steps · 8 as scripted · no spend recorded`. If either fails, stop — nothing\nbelow is meaningful on a broken baseline.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Claude subscription account\n\nThe local POC defaults to Claude Code using `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Keep that\ntoken in the machine-level secrets file, not this project's `.env`, and source\nthe machine-level file before running the commands below.\n\nCheck what is actually in play:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python authcheck.py\n```\n\nExpected: `Provider: Claude Code subscription account`, the token marked set,\nand Claude reporting logged in. The diagnostic never prints the token.\n\n`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` remains an opt-in compatibility path for\nAPI deployments, but it is not the local POC path.\n\nThe subscription route is pinned to `claude-sonnet-4-6`; the harness passes\nthat concrete model to `claude --model` and records it in reports.\n`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL` is an explicit experimental override. Changing it starts\na different evaluation and cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another\nmodel.\n\nThen, in order — each step is cheap and each one gates the next:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live -m live -q\n```\n\nThree cases and a control-envelope check using account-plan quota. Claude CLI\ndoes return cache counters (`cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`)\nand a per-model `modelUsage` breakdown, and the harness now records them via\n`harness/claude_account_cli.py::_request_usage` into `RequestUsage`; the\nAnthropic SDK-only cache-counter test remains skipped for account mode pending\na captured live sample to enable that assertion, not because the CLI lacks the\ncounters. A pass here is the first evidence that the local account path works\nend to end.\n\nStart with the cases that exposed request and routing instability:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-01 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-03 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-04 \\\n  --max-trials 3\n```\n\nContinue the same checkpoint in a later account window using the path printed\nby the runner:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --resume logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json --max-trials 3\n```\n\nOnly after those cases are reliable, run the broad suite in bounded chunks:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 --max-trials 12\n```\n\nThe targeted run and later broad chunks report pass@k (capability) and pass^k\n(reliability) on stub envelopes. This consumes account-plan quota rather than\nmetered API spend.\n**Read pass^k, not pass@k** — a case at\npass@3 = 1.0 and pass^3 = 0.33 is a coin toss with good luck. Exits non-zero if\nany case is unreliable, and names them.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 5 --pressure\n```\n\nThe O-10 probe: five total trials per selected case, rotating across five\nred-team softening phrasings (\"skip the caveats\", \"don't hedge\"). The graders\nstill run, but **a pass here only means the mechanical rules held.** Whether the\nsurrounding prose *undercut* the limitations is not automatable — open the\n`*-transcripts.json` beside the report and read them. That reading is the whole\npoint of the run.\n\nA definitive Claude subscription limit stops either evaluation immediately and\nprints a resume command. Only fully completed cases enter pass@k/pass^k; partial\ntrials remain in the checkpoint for diagnosis and continuation.\n\nThe default whole-call deadline remains 120 seconds. The Claude account route\nuses several sequential CLI invocations, so latency investigations may widen\nthat control envelope without changing inference, for example:\n\n```bash\nLOOP_MAX_SECONDS=240 .venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 1 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-03\n```\n\nAn exhausted output retry now reports the final rendering-gate objection in the\neval or demo error instead of only PydanticAI's generic retry-limit message.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python demo.py --stub\n.venv/bin/python demo.py\n```\n\nThe first time a real model answers the eight questions an audience will see.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The capture — re-confirm the contract against the real emitter\n\n**The gaps this section was written for are closed.** The data project answered\nbetween sessions: G-1 (five real envelopes), G-2 (input catalog), G-3 (directory\nrecord shape), G-5, G-7 and G-8 are all marked closed in\n`contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md`, the contract moved to **v0.3.0**, and\nthe emitter is now `emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py`. `capture.py` is therefore no\nlonger closing a gap — it is the regression check that the harness and the real\nemitter still agree, which is worth running whenever either moves.\n\nPoint the harness at the data project:\n\n```bash\ngrep -q DATA_PROJECT_ROOT .env || printf 'DATA_PROJECT_ROOT=%s\\n' \"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\" >> .env\n.venv/bin/python -c \"from config import settings; print(settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER, settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER.exists())\"\n```\n\nExpected: the path to `scripts/emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py` and `True`. `.env` is\nread by this repo's settings, not by your shell, so check it this way rather than\nechoing `$DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`. If the emitter has a different filename, set\n`EVIDENCE_EMITTER_NAME` rather than editing code. Then confirm the data project\nis healthy — its emitter runs in **its own** venv, never this one:\n\n```bash\nDATA_ROOT=\"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\"\n\"$DATA_ROOT/.venv/bin/python\" \"$DATA_ROOT/scripts/test_poc_evidence.py\"\n```\n\nRehearse, then run for real:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python capture.py --stub\n.venv/bin/python capture.py\n```\n\nIt writes artefacts plus a `REPORT.md` under `captures/<timestamp>/`: the input\ncatalog, the school directory, and one envelope per `result_kind`. The envelope\nrequests are the ones the golden case set declares — not requests invented by the\ncapture script — with fixture ACARA IDs swapped for real ones from the directory\nresult. `forecast` is skipped and says why: `VC-POC-14` is\n`not_currently_supported`, a gated next-census FTE forecast awaiting a passing\nbacktest, so there is no envelope to capture.\n\n**A rejection is still a result**, and now a more interesting one: it means the\nharness and the emitter have drifted apart. `REPORT.md` records the command and\nthe emitter's own error verbatim. Exit 1 means something was missed; read it.\n\nOne measured behaviour from G-6 worth remembering when you read a capture: an\nunrecognised value in a closed-vocabulary filter key returns **exit 0 with an\nempty result, not an error**, and the emitter upper-cases filter values before\nmatching. An empty result is a data-layer signal, not confirmation the value was\nvalid.\n\nIf the catalog changed, adopt it deliberately — **all three regenerations, or\nthey disagree:**\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m prompts.build_prompt --capture\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.build_stub_fixtures\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.build_golden_cases\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n```\n\nA failing `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` after this is the pin doing its job\n(ADR-008) — adopt deliberately, never edit the pin to make it pass.\n\n---\n\n## 3. What is still open with the data project\n\nTwo of the eight gaps are not marked closed:\n\n| gap | what is still wanted | cost to them |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G-4** | The conditional entries in `required_inputs` are prose we string-split (`\"distance_km when market_definition is distance\"`). Rewording that sentence silently changes harness behaviour. A structured form would end that. | a schema change, deferred to a revision |\n| **G-6** | Partially answered — the closed-vocabulary values arrived in the response pack. What remains is confirmation that `suburbs` and `postcodes` are open sets. | one sentence |\n\nEverything else in `contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md` is marked closed\nwith the answer recorded next to it. There is no longer a document waiting to be\nsent — it has been sent and answered.\n\n---\n\n## Order, if you only do one thing\n\n`.venv/bin/python authcheck.py`. It costs a fraction of a cent, changes nothing,\nand tells you which of four things is wrong instead of leaving you to read a 401\nthat looks the same for all of them.\n","numLines":217,"startLine":1,"totalLines":217}}}
