{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W24MHfQUz9nXwPhxDAuUTe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Harness Redesign — Victorian K-12 Market Intelligence POC\n2\t\n3\t> **Status:** founding architecture · seeded from the planning phase, 2026-08-29\n4\t> This document is self-contained: it is the founding architecture of the new repository and\n5\t> assumes no access to the predecessor repo. Where it supersedes a predecessor decision it\n6\t> says so inline, once, so the history is carried without being load-bearing.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## 1. What this system is\n11\t\n12\tA natural-language front end over a **deterministic evidence contract** published by a\n13\tseparate data project. A user asks a question about the Victorian K-12 school market; a\n14\tPydanticAI agent maps it to one of the contract's approved question IDs with a validated\n15\tstructured request, invokes the data layer's emitter, and renders the returned evidence\n16\tenvelope faithfully — grade-school-honest about confidence, limitations, and what cannot\n17\tbe answered.\n18\t\n19\t**The harness never composes SQL, never touches a database, and never computes a figure.**\n20\tEvery number in every answer originates in the data layer's `result`/`evidence` payload.\n21\tThis supersedes the predecessor's design (an LLM writing SQL over a read-only marts\n22\tschema): the data project moved that entire concern behind its contract, and the harness\n23\tbecame a smaller, safer thing — an intent mapper, a slot filler, and a faithful renderer.\n24\t\n25\t**The breadth model** (carried from the predecessor, one term substituted):\n26\t\n27\t```\n28\tRange of answerable questions = f( question registry , tool surface , output contract )\n29\t```\n30\t\n31\tThe registry belongs to the data project; growing the answerable set is a contract\n32\trelease, not a harness change. The harness's own quality bar is therefore not \"can it\n33\tanswer more\" but \"does it map correctly, ask when it must, render faithfully, and refuse\n34\thonestly\".\n35\t\n36\t## 2. The contract boundary\n37\t\n38\t| Data project owns | Harness owns |\n39\t|---|---|\n40\t| Question registry (IDs, inputs, sources, joins) | NL interpretation → question ID + request |\n41\t| Deterministic computation and evidence | Conversation, clarification, rendering |\n42\t| Provenance, confidence axes, limitations text | Preserving all of those verbatim in output |\n43\t| Confidence-grade mapping (contract v0.2.0, CR-4) | Displaying the grade, never assigning one |\n44\t| Exclusion lists (what is deliberately unavailable) | Turning exclusions into honest refusals |\n45\t\n46\tInterface protocol (contract v0.2.0): subprocess invocation of\n47\t`emit_poc_evidence.py` in the **data project's own environment**; success = exit 0 +\n48\tenvelope JSON on stdout; request/data error = exit 2 + error JSON on stderr carrying a\n49\tclosed `error_kind` (`bad_request | unknown_question | excluded_question |\n50\tdata_unavailable | internal`). Two preflights: `--input-catalog` (allow-listed control\n51\tvalues) and `--school-directory` (school identity resolution). The negotiation record\n52\ttravels with the contract: `contract/HARNESS_FEEDBACK_v0.1.0.md` (our six change\n53\trequests), `contract/K12_DATA_DISCOVERY_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md` (CR-1/2 delivered, CR-3–6\n54\trefined), `contract/HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md` (the four agreements for the next\n55\trevision). Where this design depends on an open item it names it and states the\n56\tinterim behaviour.\n57\t\n58\t**Contract pinning.** The contract files are vendored under `contract/` with a SHA-256\n59\tpin file (`contract/PINNED.json`). A unit test recomputes the hashes; any drift —\n60\tincluding a v0.2.0 drop — fails the suite until the pin is deliberately regenerated and\n61\tthe golden cases re-pointed. Same Stop Signal pattern the predecessor used for source\n62\tschemas, applied to the one interface this system has.\n63\t\n64\t## 3. Repository layout (target)\n65\t\n66\t```\n67\tharness-project/\n68\t├── config/settings.py          # single config source of truth (model, budgets, paths,\n69\t│                               #   DATA_PROJECT_ROOT, cache minimums, two-tier secrets)\n70\t├── contract/                   # vendored data-project interface, pinned by hash\n71\t│   ├── poc_question_registry.v0.2.0.json\n72\t│   ├── poc_evidence_contract.v0.2.0.schema.json\n73\t│   ├── poc_evidence_error.v0.2.0.schema.json\n74\t│   ├── poc_acceptance_fixtures.v0.2.0.json\n75\t│   ├── POC_EVIDENCE_CONTRACT.md  POC_HARNESS_HANDOFF.md\n76\t│   ├── HARNESS_FEEDBACK_v0.1.0.md  K12_DATA_DISCOVERY_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md\n77\t│   ├── HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md    # the negotiation record, pinned with the artefacts\n78\t│   └── PINNED.json\n79\t├── harness/\n80\t│   ├── agent.py                # agent assembly: provider wiring, output union, budgets\n81\t│   ├── tools.py                # the three tools (§4)\n82\t│   ├── outputs.py              # the output union (§5)\n83\t│   ├── rendering.py            # envelope-faithfulness rules + grounding validator (§6)\n84\t│   ├── errors.py  retry.py  logging_config.py  usage.py    # carried modules, unchanged\n85\t├── prompts/system.md           # frozen, cached; schema block = registry summary (§8)\n86\t├── evals/                      # golden-suite machinery (carried) + new cases\n87\t├── tests/                      # unit (CI, zero network) + golden case definitions\n88\t├── sql/usage_views.sql         # telemetry views (carried)\n89\t├── docs/\n90\t│   ├── architecture.md         # this document\n91\t│   ├── decisions.md            # founding ADR log (§10)\n92\t│   ├── prd.md  prd-addendum.md # product definition, carried verbatim\n93\t├── releases/                   # merge-time versioning (carried CI contract)\n94\t└── run.py                      # CLI entry point\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\t## 4. Tool surface — exactly three tools\n98\t\n99\t1. **`search_schools(search, sector?, school_type?, limit)`** → wraps\n100\t   `--school-directory`. The only way a school becomes a subject: the agent must resolve\n101\t   the user's school name to an `acara_sml_id` here and confirm ambiguous matches with the\n102\t   user. No name-matching anywhere else.\n103\t2. **`get_input_catalog()`** → wraps `--input-catalog`. Called once at startup and cached\n104\t   for the process lifetime (it is static per contract version); its content is also\n105\t   summarised into the system prompt's schema block, so at runtime this tool exists mainly\n106\t   for the agent to double-check an unusual control value.\n107\t3. **`fetch_evidence(question_id, request)`** → wraps the emitter. On exit 2 the tool\n108\t   branches mechanically on the error envelope's `error_kind` (contract v0.2.0, handoff\n109\t   obligation 6): `bad_request` → the message is raised as `ModelRetry` so the agent\n110\t   repairs the structured request; `unknown_question` / `excluded_question` →\n111\t   short-circuit to an `Unsupported` outcome carrying the exclusion reason, never a\n112\t   retry; `data_unavailable` / `internal` → a terminal harness error (operational stop).\n113\t   A sixth kind, `unanswerable` (valid request the data cannot satisfy — no location\n114\t   record, no coordinate, no area code), is proposed for the next revision and will map\n115\t   to `Unsupported` with the reason; until then those cases arrive as `bad_request` and\n116\t   the tool caps repair attempts so an unrepairable request cannot loop.\n117\t\n118\tTool results are data, not instructions (prompt-injection posture carried: school names\n119\tand publisher text flow through envelopes; the system prompt states that tool output\n120\tnever overrides these rules, and the eval suite keeps canary-based injection cases).\n121\t\n122\t**Invocation detail.** `fetch_evidence` runs\n123\t`{DATA_PROJECT_ROOT}/.venv/bin/python {DATA_PROJECT_ROOT}/scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py`\n124\tvia `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec` with a per-call timeout from settings. Requests\n125\tabove a size threshold go through `--request-file` in a temp dir rather than argv.\n126\t`DATA_PROJECT_ROOT` (and an optional `DATA_PROJECT_PYTHON` override) live in\n127\t`config/settings.py`. This is deliberately the contract's own protocol; an in-process\n128\timport of the emitter is a later optimisation and would be a recorded decision, not a\n129\tdrift.\n130\t\n131\t## 5. Output contract — a four-branch union\n132\t\n133\t```python\n134\tHarnessOutput = RenderedAnswer | ClarificationNeeded | Unsupported | BudgetExceeded\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\t- **`RenderedAnswer`** — prose + the preserved envelope. Fields: `answer` (the narrative),\n138\t  `question_id`, `contract_version`, `evidence`, `provenance`, `confidence`,\n139\t  `limitations` (verbatim list from the envelope), `deterministic_signals`,\n140\t  `data_status_note` (harness-derived until CR-3: what came back empty/gappy).\n141\t  Validators enforce: limitations non-empty when the envelope carried any; every one of\n142\t  the six preserved fields present; the grounding rule (§6).\n143\t- **`ClarificationNeeded`** — the agent is missing a *material* input it must not invent.\n144\t  Fields: `question_id` (tentative), `missing` (list of {input, why_material,\n145\t  allowed_values from the catalog}), `prompt_to_user`. Produced by the agent choosing this\n146\t  branch — but *gated* by a harness-side materials list (§7), so the model can neither\n147\t  skip asking nor ask about defaultable trivia.\n148\t- **`Unsupported`** — the honest refusal. Fields: `reason_kind`\n149\t  (`excluded_by_contract | not_in_registry | out_of_scope | not_yet_validated`), `reason`\n150\t  (for contract exclusions: the exclusion text itself), `nearest_supported` (optional\n151\t  pointer to a question the registry *can* answer). Generated from the contract's\n152\t  `excluded_questions` and deliberately-unavailable lists — refusals are contract data,\n153\t  not model judgement. `not_yet_validated` is the v0.3.0 case: a capability that is\n154\t  registered but disabled pending a passing local backtest (VC-POC-14). It must never be\n155\t  rendered as \"we do not answer that\" — the honest statement is that the capability\n156\t  exists and has not yet earned its grade.\n157\t- **`BudgetExceeded`** — produced by the harness when the control envelope trips (§9),\n158\t  never selected by the model. The agent's `output_type` is the first three branches;\n159\t  `run_harness()` widens the return type.\n160\t\n161\t## 6. Rendering rules (envelope faithfulness)\n162\t\n163\tThese are enforced in `rendering.py` as code and in the eval graders — not requested in\n164\tthe prompt and hoped for:\n165\t\n166\t1. **Grounding.** Every number in `answer` must appear in the envelope's\n167\t   `result`/`evidence` (or in the user's own question). A number that appears nowhere\n168\t   fails validation → `ModelRetry`. (Carried mechanism; the grader half already exists.)\n169\t2. **Limitations travel verbatim.** The envelope's `limitations` strings are rendered\n170\t   as-is, never paraphrased, never dropped. Prose may *add* context; it may not soften.\n171\t3. **Signals are calculations, not conclusions.** A `deterministic_signal` renders as its\n172\t   disclosed rule (\"largest returned value for X in year Y\") — never as a recommendation,\n173\t   ranking, or cause.\n174\t4. **Context is not forecast.** VIF projections and building approvals (VC-POC-13) render\n175\t   with their returned caveats and are never presented as an enrolment forecast, capacity\n176\t   estimate, or demand claim.\n177\t4a. **A forecast renders only when it has earned its grade.** For the gated enrolment\n178\t   outlook (VC-POC-14, v0.3.0): a `Modelled` answer renders only with its passing backtest\n179\t   artifact reference and applicable stratum — a response claiming Modelled without them\n180\t   is treated as invalid, not rendered. Required disclosures render verbatim from the\n181\t   envelope. The horizon is stated as the next annual census with the **actual**\n182\t   as-of-to-census lead time from the resolved request; \"next year\", \"twelve months\" and\n183\t   equivalents are forbidden phrasings, enforced by a deterministic validator and\n184\t   red-team cases, because a model mirrors the framing of the question it was asked.\n185\t5. **Confidence renders as given.** Interim (pre-CR-4): the four axis ratings are shown\n186\t   verbatim; the harness displays **no** five-grade label, because it has no authority to\n187\t   assign one. Post-CR-4 (agreed shape — `contract/HARNESS_REPLY_TO_DATA_DISCOVERY_v0.2.0.md`):\n188\t   `grade.value` + `weakest_input` render as the headline; compound answers render each\n189\t   component's own grade; a `Modelled` figure renders with the `backtest` block that\n190\t   earned it; and the `claim_eligibility` field gates the **language** — no trend wording\n191\t   when `trend` is ineligible, and the PRD's \"directional, not decision-grade\" framing\n192\t   whenever `decision_grade` is false. Coverage never changes a figure's grade; it is\n193\t   reported in `data_status` and constrains claims.\n194\t6. **Empty is stated.** Until CR-3, the harness inspects `result.data` and states plainly\n195\t   when a series came back empty or gappy, at the point where the number would have been.\n196\t\n197\t## 7. Clarification flow (new capability vs the predecessor)\n198\t\n199\tThe contract's handoff obliges the harness to **ask the user** for a missing material\n200\tchoice rather than assume it. Materials list (interim, hardcoded in\n201\t`config/settings.py` as `MATERIAL_INPUTS` keyed by question ID, until CR-5 ships\n202\tper-question request schemas — policy agreed in `contract/HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md`\n203\t§4): `market_definition` (05–07), `distance_km` (05–07 when the market is distance;\n204\t08 always), `grades` (07 only — the grade asked about *is* the question),\n205\t`peer_filters` (09), `segment_filters` (10), `sa2_codes` (12–13). **Year range is\n206\tnever material**: the full available span is the honest default and the rendered\n207\tanswer shows the span actually applied (from the envelope's resolved filters), which\n208\tsatisfies the product rule that a trajectory displays its real span without a\n209\tclarification on every question. ERP age/sex, SEIFA selectors, metrics and ratios\n210\tlikewise default and are rendered as applied.\n211\t\n212\tFlow: `ask()` returns `ClarificationNeeded`; the caller (CLI now, HTTP later) presents\n213\t`prompt_to_user`, collects the answer, and re-invokes with the prior message history plus\n214\tthe user's reply — PydanticAI message history carries the state; no bespoke session store\n215\tfor the POC. One clarification round-trip is the budgeted norm; a second consumes the\n216\tsame step budget as any other iteration (§9). Defaultable inputs (metrics selection,\n217\tSEIFA index) are passed through without ceremony and the applied values rendered from the\n218\tenvelope's `evidence[].filters`.\n219\t\n220\t## 8. System prompt and caching\n221\t\n222\tOne frozen prompt (`prompts/system.md`), byte-exact for prompt caching, structured as:\n223\trules block (rendering rules §6 in prompt form, the ask-don't-assume obligation, the\n224\tinjection posture) + **schema block** = a generated summary of the pinned registry (per\n225\tquestion: ID, purpose, required/material/optional inputs, result kind) + the input\n226\tcatalog's allow-lists. The schema block is *generated from* `contract/` by a script at\n227\tbuild time, so prompt and contract cannot drift; regenerating it is part of a contract\n228\tbump. Nothing request-scoped (timestamps, IDs, user text) enters the cached prefix.\n229\tPer-model cache minimums live in `config/settings.py` and are re-verified on model\n230\tupgrades; the cache regression check is `cache_read_tokens > 0` in the usage telemetry.\n231\t\n232\t**Model:** `claude-sonnet-4-6` (carried default). The task — intent classification,\n233\tslot-filling, faithful narration — is well inside Sonnet's envelope; a Haiku routing tier\n234\tis a later cost optimisation, not a POC concern.\n235\t\n236\t## 9. Control envelope, retry, errors, telemetry (carried invariants)\n237\t\n238\tUnchanged from the proven modules, which are carried as files, not rewritten:\n239\t\n240\t- **Retry:** exactly one owner (`harness/retry.py`, Tenacity); the Anthropic SDK client\n241\t  is constructed with `max_retries=0`. Transient/terminal classification lives on the\n242\t  exception types (`harness/errors.py`).\n243\t- **Budgets:** `UsageLimits` (steps/tool calls) + `asyncio.wait_for` (wall clock) +\n244\t  measured spend, enforced in `ask()`; a breach returns typed `BudgetExceeded` with what\n245\t  was learned so far — never a crash. The evidence subprocess gets its own timeout.\n246\t- **Auth:** API-key or account-bearer-token, auto-detected; two-tier secrets (in-repo\n247\t  `.env` over a shared machine-level file via `SHARED_ENV_FILE`).\n248\t- **Telemetry:** one JSONL line per LLM request + one per run\n249\t  (`logs/usage/usage-YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl`), read back through in-memory DuckDB views\n250\t  (`sql/usage_views.sql`). The telemetry path never opens any other database.\n251\t\n252\t## 10. Founding decision log (seeded into `docs/decisions.md`)\n253\t\n254\t| # | Decision | Notes |\n255\t|---|---|---|\n256\t| ADR-001 | The evidence contract is the **only** data interface: no SQL, no DB access, no model arithmetic | Supersedes the predecessor's text-to-SQL agent design (its ADR-0002/0013); those concerns moved behind the data project's contract |\n257\t| ADR-002 | PydanticAI, union `output_type`, tools coexisting with typed output | Carried; chosen originally because Instructor's response-model evicts action tools, which forces hallucinated numbers into a schema that validates |\n258\t| ADR-003 | Single retry owner (Tenacity), SDK retries 0 | Carried |\n259\t| ADR-004 | Control envelope enforced in code; typed `BudgetExceeded` | Carried |\n260\t| ADR-005 | Usage/cost telemetry: JSONL append + DuckDB views at read time | Carried |\n261\t| ADR-006 | Frozen cached system prompt; per-model cache minimums in settings; schema block generated from the pinned contract | Carried + extended |\n262\t| ADR-007 | Eval-first: the golden suite exists before the agent answers a real question; graders read transcripts, never the agent's self-report | Carried |\n263\t| ADR-008 | Contract pinned by hash; a bump is a loud failure until re-pointed | New |\n264\t| ADR-009 | Confidence renders as the data layer states it; the harness never assigns a grade (interim: axes only, pending contract CR-4) | New |\n265\t| ADR-010 | POC product surface is enrolment / market-position intelligence; finance is excluded by the contract | Supersedes the predecessor's finance-benchmark lead demo (its ADR-0023); consistent with the PRD conceding financial benchmarking to the incumbent |\n266\t| ADR-011 | Two-tier secrets; dual auth mode | Carried |\n267\t\n268\t## 11. Eval design\n269\t\n270\tMachinery carried (schema/fixtures/runner/graders pattern; deterministic tier on every\n271\tPR at zero network cost, live k-trial tier manual with pass@k / pass^k). What changes is\n272\tthe **fixture substrate and the graders' targets**:\n273\t\n274\t- A golden case = NL phrasing(s) + expected `question_id` + expected request (with\n275\t  tolerance for equivalent orderings) + direction\n276\t  (`should_answer | should_clarify | should_refuse | should_resist_injection`).\n277\t- **Fixture:** a stub emitter — a small script satisfying the same CLI contract, serving\n278\t  canned envelopes from fixture JSON (and canned exit-2 errors). Golden runs never need\n279\t  the real data project; the acceptance suite against the *real* emitter is the data\n280\t  project's own `test_poc_evidence.py`, run at integration time.\n281\t- **Graders (deterministic only, carried posture):** chosen-question match; request\n282\t  match; envelope preservation (six fields intact, limitations verbatim); grounding\n283\t  (numbers trace to envelope); clarification correctness (material input missing →\n284\t  `ClarificationNeeded` naming it, and *not* asking when nothing material is missing);\n285\t  refusal correctness (excluded topics → `Unsupported` with `excluded_by_contract`);\n286\t  canary non-reproduction for injection cases.\n287\t- **Case sources:** one should-answer case per registry question (15); should-clarify\n288\t  cases per material input; should-refuse cases generated from the contract's\n289\t  `excluded_questions` + deliberately-unavailable lists (transport, finance, catchments,\n290\t  crosswalks…); injection cases seeded with canaries in stub-envelope school names and\n291\t  limitation strings.\n292\t\n293\t## 12. Build order (the new repo's first milestones)\n294\t\n295\t1. **M1 — seed verification:** carried modules' unit tests green; contract pin test\n296\t   green; stub emitter runs.\n297\t2. **M2 — golden cases first:** author the case set (§11) against the stub; graders\n298\t   green on reference solutions before any agent exists.\n299\t3. **M3 — tools + agent assembly:** the three tools, output union, rendering validators;\n300\t   FunctionModel-scripted loop tests for the mechanical guardrails (repair-on-exit-2,\n301\t   refusal short-circuit, budget trip).\n302\t4. **M4 — prompt + live tier:** generate the schema block, freeze the prompt, run the\n303\t   live eval tier against real credentials and the real emitter; error analysis grows the\n304\t   case set.\n305\t5. **M5 — demo script:** a walked end-to-end demo across the four safe question groups\n306\t   (school evidence, cohorts/market, area context, reference), each answer showing\n307\t   provenance + confidence + limitations.\n308\t\n309\t## 13. Open items for the owner (recommendations attached)\n310\t\n311\t1. **Demo scope ratification.** ADR-010 records that the POC demo is enrolment /\n312\t   market-position, not finance. Recommend: ratify (it follows from the contract and the\n313\t   PRD §15 concession); revisit only when the data project ships a finance-bearing\n314\t   contract version.\n315\t2. **Clarification UX budget.** Recommend: at most one clarification round-trip per\n316\t   question in the demo script; a question still ambiguous after one round renders as\n317\t   `Unsupported` with guidance. Adjustable in settings.\n318\t3. **Server layer timing.** The carried template includes a FastAPI scaffold. Recommend:\n319\t   leave it out of M1–M5 (the POC is CLI + evals); wire it when a demo needs a UI.\n320\t4. **Next contract revision (CR-3…CR-6) adoption.** v0.2.0 is adopted now (CR-1/2\n321\t   delivered). When the data project ships the agreed revision, the pin test fails by\n322\t   design. Recommend: adopt in one change — re-pin, regenerate the schema block, delete\n323\t   the three interim shims (hardcoded materials list, harness-side empty/partial\n324\t   detection, axis-only confidence rendering), re-point golden cases.\n325\t5. **Short-horizon enrolment outlook (owner decision).** The data project proposes one\n326\t   narrow, backtest-gated `Modelled` capability so the POC exercises the confidence gate\n327\t   rather than only governed retrieval. It reopens the PRD's MVP deferral of forecasting\n328\t   (§11.2) at a cost borne by the data project. Harness exposure is nil (one more\n329\t   registry question, rendered through the same envelope). Recommend: approve as framed\n330\t   — registered disabled, promoted only by a recorded passing backtest, abstention the\n331\t   normal outcome — with the harness requirements stated in\n332\t   `contract/HARNESS_REPLY_TO_DATA_DISCOVERY_v0.2.0.md` §5.\n333\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c0ed0a-c13a-40ee-817d-fb81fa072daa","uuid":"d3011846-a10e-4dfd-a5fe-96ef9e6d9de5","timestamp":"2026-09-29T07:34:34.089Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/docs/architecture.md","content":"# Harness Redesign — Victorian K-12 Market Intelligence POC\n\n> **Status:** founding architecture · seeded from the planning phase, 2026-08-29\n> This document is self-contained: it is the founding architecture of the new repository and\n> assumes no access to the predecessor repo. Where it supersedes a predecessor decision it\n> says so inline, once, so the history is carried without being load-bearing.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What this system is\n\nA natural-language front end over a **deterministic evidence contract** published by a\nseparate data project. A user asks a question about the Victorian K-12 school market; a\nPydanticAI agent maps it to one of the contract's approved question IDs with a validated\nstructured request, invokes the data layer's emitter, and renders the returned evidence\nenvelope faithfully — grade-school-honest about confidence, limitations, and what cannot\nbe answered.\n\n**The harness never composes SQL, never touches a database, and never computes a figure.**\nEvery number in every answer originates in the data layer's `result`/`evidence` payload.\nThis supersedes the predecessor's design (an LLM writing SQL over a read-only marts\nschema): the data project moved that entire concern behind its contract, and the harness\nbecame a smaller, safer thing — an intent mapper, a slot filler, and a faithful renderer.\n\n**The breadth model** (carried from the predecessor, one term substituted):\n\n```\nRange of answerable questions = f( question registry , tool surface , output contract )\n```\n\nThe registry belongs to the data project; growing the answerable set is a contract\nrelease, not a harness change. The harness's own quality bar is therefore not \"can it\nanswer more\" but \"does it map correctly, ask when it must, render faithfully, and refuse\nhonestly\".\n\n## 2. The contract boundary\n\n| Data project owns | Harness owns |\n|---|---|\n| Question registry (IDs, inputs, sources, joins) | NL interpretation → question ID + request |\n| Deterministic computation and evidence | Conversation, clarification, rendering |\n| Provenance, confidence axes, limitations text | Preserving all of those verbatim in output |\n| Confidence-grade mapping (contract v0.2.0, CR-4) | Displaying the grade, never assigning one |\n| Exclusion lists (what is deliberately unavailable) | Turning exclusions into honest refusals |\n\nInterface protocol (contract v0.2.0): subprocess invocation of\n`emit_poc_evidence.py` in the **data project's own environment**; success = exit 0 +\nenvelope JSON on stdout; request/data error = exit 2 + error JSON on stderr carrying a\nclosed `error_kind` (`bad_request | unknown_question | excluded_question |\ndata_unavailable | internal`). Two preflights: `--input-catalog` (allow-listed control\nvalues) and `--school-directory` (school identity resolution). The negotiation record\ntravels with the contract: `contract/HARNESS_FEEDBACK_v0.1.0.md` (our six change\nrequests), `contract/K12_DATA_DISCOVERY_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md` (CR-1/2 delivered, CR-3–6\nrefined), `contract/HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md` (the four agreements for the next\nrevision). Where this design depends on an open item it names it and states the\ninterim behaviour.\n\n**Contract pinning.** The contract files are vendored under `contract/` with a SHA-256\npin file (`contract/PINNED.json`). A unit test recomputes the hashes; any drift —\nincluding a v0.2.0 drop — fails the suite until the pin is deliberately regenerated and\nthe golden cases re-pointed. Same Stop Signal pattern the predecessor used for source\nschemas, applied to the one interface this system has.\n\n## 3. Repository layout (target)\n\n```\nharness-project/\n├── config/settings.py          # single config source of truth (model, budgets, paths,\n│                               #   DATA_PROJECT_ROOT, cache minimums, two-tier secrets)\n├── contract/                   # vendored data-project interface, pinned by hash\n│   ├── poc_question_registry.v0.2.0.json\n│   ├── poc_evidence_contract.v0.2.0.schema.json\n│   ├── poc_evidence_error.v0.2.0.schema.json\n│   ├── poc_acceptance_fixtures.v0.2.0.json\n│   ├── POC_EVIDENCE_CONTRACT.md  POC_HARNESS_HANDOFF.md\n│   ├── HARNESS_FEEDBACK_v0.1.0.md  K12_DATA_DISCOVERY_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md\n│   ├── HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md    # the negotiation record, pinned with the artefacts\n│   └── PINNED.json\n├── harness/\n│   ├── agent.py                # agent assembly: provider wiring, output union, budgets\n│   ├── tools.py                # the three tools (§4)\n│   ├── outputs.py              # the output union (§5)\n│   ├── rendering.py            # envelope-faithfulness rules + grounding validator (§6)\n│   ├── errors.py  retry.py  logging_config.py  usage.py    # carried modules, unchanged\n├── prompts/system.md           # frozen, cached; schema block = registry summary (§8)\n├── evals/                      # golden-suite machinery (carried) + new cases\n├── tests/                      # unit (CI, zero network) + golden case definitions\n├── sql/usage_views.sql         # telemetry views (carried)\n├── docs/\n│   ├── architecture.md         # this document\n│   ├── decisions.md            # founding ADR log (§10)\n│   ├── prd.md  prd-addendum.md # product definition, carried verbatim\n├── releases/                   # merge-time versioning (carried CI contract)\n└── run.py                      # CLI entry point\n```\n\n## 4. Tool surface — exactly three tools\n\n1. **`search_schools(search, sector?, school_type?, limit)`** → wraps\n   `--school-directory`. The only way a school becomes a subject: the agent must resolve\n   the user's school name to an `acara_sml_id` here and confirm ambiguous matches with the\n   user. No name-matching anywhere else.\n2. **`get_input_catalog()`** → wraps `--input-catalog`. Called once at startup and cached\n   for the process lifetime (it is static per contract version); its content is also\n   summarised into the system prompt's schema block, so at runtime this tool exists mainly\n   for the agent to double-check an unusual control value.\n3. **`fetch_evidence(question_id, request)`** → wraps the emitter. On exit 2 the tool\n   branches mechanically on the error envelope's `error_kind` (contract v0.2.0, handoff\n   obligation 6): `bad_request` → the message is raised as `ModelRetry` so the agent\n   repairs the structured request; `unknown_question` / `excluded_question` →\n   short-circuit to an `Unsupported` outcome carrying the exclusion reason, never a\n   retry; `data_unavailable` / `internal` → a terminal harness error (operational stop).\n   A sixth kind, `unanswerable` (valid request the data cannot satisfy — no location\n   record, no coordinate, no area code), is proposed for the next revision and will map\n   to `Unsupported` with the reason; until then those cases arrive as `bad_request` and\n   the tool caps repair attempts so an unrepairable request cannot loop.\n\nTool results are data, not instructions (prompt-injection posture carried: school names\nand publisher text flow through envelopes; the system prompt states that tool output\nnever overrides these rules, and the eval suite keeps canary-based injection cases).\n\n**Invocation detail.** `fetch_evidence` runs\n`{DATA_PROJECT_ROOT}/.venv/bin/python {DATA_PROJECT_ROOT}/scripts/emit_poc_evidence.py`\nvia `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec` with a per-call timeout from settings. Requests\nabove a size threshold go through `--request-file` in a temp dir rather than argv.\n`DATA_PROJECT_ROOT` (and an optional `DATA_PROJECT_PYTHON` override) live in\n`config/settings.py`. This is deliberately the contract's own protocol; an in-process\nimport of the emitter is a later optimisation and would be a recorded decision, not a\ndrift.\n\n## 5. Output contract — a four-branch union\n\n```python\nHarnessOutput = RenderedAnswer | ClarificationNeeded | Unsupported | BudgetExceeded\n```\n\n- **`RenderedAnswer`** — prose + the preserved envelope. Fields: `answer` (the narrative),\n  `question_id`, `contract_version`, `evidence`, `provenance`, `confidence`,\n  `limitations` (verbatim list from the envelope), `deterministic_signals`,\n  `data_status_note` (harness-derived until CR-3: what came back empty/gappy).\n  Validators enforce: limitations non-empty when the envelope carried any; every one of\n  the six preserved fields present; the grounding rule (§6).\n- **`ClarificationNeeded`** — the agent is missing a *material* input it must not invent.\n  Fields: `question_id` (tentative), `missing` (list of {input, why_material,\n  allowed_values from the catalog}), `prompt_to_user`. Produced by the agent choosing this\n  branch — but *gated* by a harness-side materials list (§7), so the model can neither\n  skip asking nor ask about defaultable trivia.\n- **`Unsupported`** — the honest refusal. Fields: `reason_kind`\n  (`excluded_by_contract | not_in_registry | out_of_scope | not_yet_validated`), `reason`\n  (for contract exclusions: the exclusion text itself), `nearest_supported` (optional\n  pointer to a question the registry *can* answer). Generated from the contract's\n  `excluded_questions` and deliberately-unavailable lists — refusals are contract data,\n  not model judgement. `not_yet_validated` is the v0.3.0 case: a capability that is\n  registered but disabled pending a passing local backtest (VC-POC-14). It must never be\n  rendered as \"we do not answer that\" — the honest statement is that the capability\n  exists and has not yet earned its grade.\n- **`BudgetExceeded`** — produced by the harness when the control envelope trips (§9),\n  never selected by the model. The agent's `output_type` is the first three branches;\n  `run_harness()` widens the return type.\n\n## 6. Rendering rules (envelope faithfulness)\n\nThese are enforced in `rendering.py` as code and in the eval graders — not requested in\nthe prompt and hoped for:\n\n1. **Grounding.** Every number in `answer` must appear in the envelope's\n   `result`/`evidence` (or in the user's own question). A number that appears nowhere\n   fails validation → `ModelRetry`. (Carried mechanism; the grader half already exists.)\n2. **Limitations travel verbatim.** The envelope's `limitations` strings are rendered\n   as-is, never paraphrased, never dropped. Prose may *add* context; it may not soften.\n3. **Signals are calculations, not conclusions.** A `deterministic_signal` renders as its\n   disclosed rule (\"largest returned value for X in year Y\") — never as a recommendation,\n   ranking, or cause.\n4. **Context is not forecast.** VIF projections and building approvals (VC-POC-13) render\n   with their returned caveats and are never presented as an enrolment forecast, capacity\n   estimate, or demand claim.\n4a. **A forecast renders only when it has earned its grade.** For the gated enrolment\n   outlook (VC-POC-14, v0.3.0): a `Modelled` answer renders only with its passing backtest\n   artifact reference and applicable stratum — a response claiming Modelled without them\n   is treated as invalid, not rendered. Required disclosures render verbatim from the\n   envelope. The horizon is stated as the next annual census with the **actual**\n   as-of-to-census lead time from the resolved request; \"next year\", \"twelve months\" and\n   equivalents are forbidden phrasings, enforced by a deterministic validator and\n   red-team cases, because a model mirrors the framing of the question it was asked.\n5. **Confidence renders as given.** Interim (pre-CR-4): the four axis ratings are shown\n   verbatim; the harness displays **no** five-grade label, because it has no authority to\n   assign one. Post-CR-4 (agreed shape — `contract/HARNESS_REPLY_TO_DATA_DISCOVERY_v0.2.0.md`):\n   `grade.value` + `weakest_input` render as the headline; compound answers render each\n   component's own grade; a `Modelled` figure renders with the `backtest` block that\n   earned it; and the `claim_eligibility` field gates the **language** — no trend wording\n   when `trend` is ineligible, and the PRD's \"directional, not decision-grade\" framing\n   whenever `decision_grade` is false. Coverage never changes a figure's grade; it is\n   reported in `data_status` and constrains claims.\n6. **Empty is stated.** Until CR-3, the harness inspects `result.data` and states plainly\n   when a series came back empty or gappy, at the point where the number would have been.\n\n## 7. Clarification flow (new capability vs the predecessor)\n\nThe contract's handoff obliges the harness to **ask the user** for a missing material\nchoice rather than assume it. Materials list (interim, hardcoded in\n`config/settings.py` as `MATERIAL_INPUTS` keyed by question ID, until CR-5 ships\nper-question request schemas — policy agreed in `contract/HARNESS_RESPONSE_v0.2.0.md`\n§4): `market_definition` (05–07), `distance_km` (05–07 when the market is distance;\n08 always), `grades` (07 only — the grade asked about *is* the question),\n`peer_filters` (09), `segment_filters` (10), `sa2_codes` (12–13). **Year range is\nnever material**: the full available span is the honest default and the rendered\nanswer shows the span actually applied (from the envelope's resolved filters), which\nsatisfies the product rule that a trajectory displays its real span without a\nclarification on every question. ERP age/sex, SEIFA selectors, metrics and ratios\nlikewise default and are rendered as applied.\n\nFlow: `ask()` returns `ClarificationNeeded`; the caller (CLI now, HTTP later) presents\n`prompt_to_user`, collects the answer, and re-invokes with the prior message history plus\nthe user's reply — PydanticAI message history carries the state; no bespoke session store\nfor the POC. One clarification round-trip is the budgeted norm; a second consumes the\nsame step budget as any other iteration (§9). Defaultable inputs (metrics selection,\nSEIFA index) are passed through without ceremony and the applied values rendered from the\nenvelope's `evidence[].filters`.\n\n## 8. System prompt and caching\n\nOne frozen prompt (`prompts/system.md`), byte-exact for prompt caching, structured as:\nrules block (rendering rules §6 in prompt form, the ask-don't-assume obligation, the\ninjection posture) + **schema block** = a generated summary of the pinned registry (per\nquestion: ID, purpose, required/material/optional inputs, result kind) + the input\ncatalog's allow-lists. The schema block is *generated from* `contract/` by a script at\nbuild time, so prompt and contract cannot drift; regenerating it is part of a contract\nbump. Nothing request-scoped (timestamps, IDs, user text) enters the cached prefix.\nPer-model cache minimums live in `config/settings.py` and are re-verified on model\nupgrades; the cache regression check is `cache_read_tokens > 0` in the usage telemetry.\n\n**Model:** `claude-sonnet-4-6` (carried default). The task — intent classification,\nslot-filling, faithful narration — is well inside Sonnet's envelope; a Haiku routing tier\nis a later cost optimisation, not a POC concern.\n\n## 9. Control envelope, retry, errors, telemetry (carried invariants)\n\nUnchanged from the proven modules, which are carried as files, not rewritten:\n\n- **Retry:** exactly one owner (`harness/retry.py`, Tenacity); the Anthropic SDK client\n  is constructed with `max_retries=0`. Transient/terminal classification lives on the\n  exception types (`harness/errors.py`).\n- **Budgets:** `UsageLimits` (steps/tool calls) + `asyncio.wait_for` (wall clock) +\n  measured spend, enforced in `ask()`; a breach returns typed `BudgetExceeded` with what\n  was learned so far — never a crash. The evidence subprocess gets its own timeout.\n- **Auth:** API-key or account-bearer-token, auto-detected; two-tier secrets (in-repo\n  `.env` over a shared machine-level file via `SHARED_ENV_FILE`).\n- **Telemetry:** one JSONL line per LLM request + one per run\n  (`logs/usage/usage-YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl`), read back through in-memory DuckDB views\n  (`sql/usage_views.sql`). The telemetry path never opens any other database.\n\n## 10. Founding decision log (seeded into `docs/decisions.md`)\n\n| # | Decision | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| ADR-001 | The evidence contract is the **only** data interface: no SQL, no DB access, no model arithmetic | Supersedes the predecessor's text-to-SQL agent design (its ADR-0002/0013); those concerns moved behind the data project's contract |\n| ADR-002 | PydanticAI, union `output_type`, tools coexisting with typed output | Carried; chosen originally because Instructor's response-model evicts action tools, which forces hallucinated numbers into a schema that validates |\n| ADR-003 | Single retry owner (Tenacity), SDK retries 0 | Carried |\n| ADR-004 | Control envelope enforced in code; typed `BudgetExceeded` | Carried |\n| ADR-005 | Usage/cost telemetry: JSONL append + DuckDB views at read time | Carried |\n| ADR-006 | Frozen cached system prompt; per-model cache minimums in settings; schema block generated from the pinned contract | Carried + extended |\n| ADR-007 | Eval-first: the golden suite exists before the agent answers a real question; graders read transcripts, never the agent's self-report | Carried |\n| ADR-008 | Contract pinned by hash; a bump is a loud failure until re-pointed | New |\n| ADR-009 | Confidence renders as the data layer states it; the harness never assigns a grade (interim: axes only, pending contract CR-4) | New |\n| ADR-010 | POC product surface is enrolment / market-position intelligence; finance is excluded by the contract | Supersedes the predecessor's finance-benchmark lead demo (its ADR-0023); consistent with the PRD conceding financial benchmarking to the incumbent |\n| ADR-011 | Two-tier secrets; dual auth mode | Carried |\n\n## 11. Eval design\n\nMachinery carried (schema/fixtures/runner/graders pattern; deterministic tier on every\nPR at zero network cost, live k-trial tier manual with pass@k / pass^k). What changes is\nthe **fixture substrate and the graders' targets**:\n\n- A golden case = NL phrasing(s) + expected `question_id` + expected request (with\n  tolerance for equivalent orderings) + direction\n  (`should_answer | should_clarify | should_refuse | should_resist_injection`).\n- **Fixture:** a stub emitter — a small script satisfying the same CLI contract, serving\n  canned envelopes from fixture JSON (and canned exit-2 errors). Golden runs never need\n  the real data project; the acceptance suite against the *real* emitter is the data\n  project's own `test_poc_evidence.py`, run at integration time.\n- **Graders (deterministic only, carried posture):** chosen-question match; request\n  match; envelope preservation (six fields intact, limitations verbatim); grounding\n  (numbers trace to envelope); clarification correctness (material input missing →\n  `ClarificationNeeded` naming it, and *not* asking when nothing material is missing);\n  refusal correctness (excluded topics → `Unsupported` with `excluded_by_contract`);\n  canary non-reproduction for injection cases.\n- **Case sources:** one should-answer case per registry question (15); should-clarify\n  cases per material input; should-refuse cases generated from the contract's\n  `excluded_questions` + deliberately-unavailable lists (transport, finance, catchments,\n  crosswalks…); injection cases seeded with canaries in stub-envelope school names and\n  limitation strings.\n\n## 12. Build order (the new repo's first milestones)\n\n1. **M1 — seed verification:** carried modules' unit tests green; contract pin test\n   green; stub emitter runs.\n2. **M2 — golden cases first:** author the case set (§11) against the stub; graders\n   green on reference solutions before any agent exists.\n3. **M3 — tools + agent assembly:** the three tools, output union, rendering validators;\n   FunctionModel-scripted loop tests for the mechanical guardrails (repair-on-exit-2,\n   refusal short-circuit, budget trip).\n4. **M4 — prompt + live tier:** generate the schema block, freeze the prompt, run the\n   live eval tier against real credentials and the real emitter; error analysis grows the\n   case set.\n5. **M5 — demo script:** a walked end-to-end demo across the four safe question groups\n   (school evidence, cohorts/market, area context, reference), each answer showing\n   provenance + confidence + limitations.\n\n## 13. Open items for the owner (recommendations attached)\n\n1. **Demo scope ratification.** ADR-010 records that the POC demo is enrolment /\n   market-position, not finance. Recommend: ratify (it follows from the contract and the\n   PRD §15 concession); revisit only when the data project ships a finance-bearing\n   contract version.\n2. **Clarification UX budget.** Recommend: at most one clarification round-trip per\n   question in the demo script; a question still ambiguous after one round renders as\n   `Unsupported` with guidance. Adjustable in settings.\n3. **Server layer timing.** The carried template includes a FastAPI scaffold. Recommend:\n   leave it out of M1–M5 (the POC is CLI + evals); wire it when a demo needs a UI.\n4. **Next contract revision (CR-3…CR-6) adoption.** v0.2.0 is adopted now (CR-1/2\n   delivered). When the data project ships the agreed revision, the pin test fails by\n   design. Recommend: adopt in one change — re-pin, regenerate the schema block, delete\n   the three interim shims (hardcoded materials list, harness-side empty/partial\n   detection, axis-only confidence rendering), re-point golden cases.\n5. **Short-horizon enrolment outlook (owner decision).** The data project proposes one\n   narrow, backtest-gated `Modelled` capability so the POC exercises the confidence gate\n   rather than only governed retrieval. It reopens the PRD's MVP deferral of forecasting\n   (§11.2) at a cost borne by the data project. Harness exposure is nil (one more\n   registry question, rendered through the same envelope). Recommend: approve as framed\n   — registered disabled, promoted only by a recorded passing backtest, abstention the\n   normal outcome — with the harness requirements stated in\n   `contract/HARNESS_REPLY_TO_DATA_DISCOVERY_v0.2.0.md` §5.\n","numLines":333,"startLine":1,"totalLines":333}}}
