{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PpWamsrssBQNq5e97wkS1i","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Runbook — what to run, in what order\n2\t\n3\tEverything in this repo is built and tested offline against contract **v0.3.0**.\n4\tWhat remains is running it against a real model, which has still never happened.\n5\t\n6\tRun from the repo root. Every command uses the venv by absolute path.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## 0. Baseline (30 seconds, no credential)\n11\t\n12\tThis is the **deterministic tier**: pytest against the stub emitter, zero network,\n13\tgating every PR (ADR-007).\n14\t\n15\t```bash\n16\tbash setup.sh\n17\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n18\t.venv/bin/python demo.py --replay\n19\t```\n20\t\n21\tExpected: the suite green, and the demo walking eight steps ending\n22\t`8 steps · 8 as scripted · no spend recorded`. If either fails, stop — nothing\n23\tbelow is meaningful on a broken baseline.\n24\t\n25\t`--replay` is one of the demo's three modes (ADR-017), each announced by a tested\n26\tbanner printed before the first step and again after the last: `--replay` (decisions\n27\treplayed from reference solutions — no model, no cost, all fixtures), `--stub` (a real\n28\tmodel, canned envelopes), and neither flag (real model, real emitter — the only mode\n29\twhere a number on screen is a claim about a school). See §1 below for `--stub` and the\n30\tlive run.\n31\t\n32\t---\n33\t\n34\t## 1. The Claude subscription account\n35\t\n36\tThe local POC defaults to Claude Code using `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Keep that\n37\ttoken in the machine-level secrets file, not this project's `.env`, and source\n38\tthe machine-level file before running the commands below.\n39\t\n40\tCheck what is actually in play:\n41\t\n42\t```bash\n43\t.venv/bin/python authcheck.py\n44\t```\n45\t\n46\tExpected: `Provider: Claude Code subscription account`, the token marked set,\n47\tand Claude reporting logged in. The diagnostic never prints the token.\n48\t\n49\tSetting `HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` is the explicit override that\n50\tselects the Anthropic SDK provider instead of `claude_account` — an opt-in\n51\tcompatibility path for API deployments that is **potentially metered** (unlike\n52\tthe subscription account route) and is not the local POC path unless set.\n53\t\n54\tThe subscription route is pinned to `claude-sonnet-4-6`; the harness passes\n55\tthat concrete model to `claude --model` and records it in reports.\n56\t`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL` is an explicit experimental override. Changing it starts\n57\ta different evaluation and cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another\n58\tmodel.\n59\t\n60\tWhat follows is the **live tier**: manual/nightly, run against real credentials and\n61\tthe real (or stub) emitter, and never a PR gate (ADR-007). It reports pass@k\n62\t(capability) and pass^k (reliability) **separately** — read pass^k, not pass@k.\n63\t\n64\tThen, in order — each step is cheap and each one gates the next:\n65\t\n66\t```bash\n67\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live -m live -q\n68\t```\n69\t\n70\tThree cases and a control-envelope check using account-plan quota. Claude CLI\n71\tdoes return cache counters (`cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`)\n72\tand a per-model `modelUsage` breakdown, and the harness now records them via\n73\t`harness/claude_account_cli.py::_request_usage` into `RequestUsage`; the\n74\tAnthropic SDK-only cache-counter test remains skipped for account mode pending\n75\ta captured live sample to enable that assertion, not because the CLI lacks the\n76\tcounters. A pass here is the first evidence that the local account path works\n77\tend to end.\n78\t\n79\tStart with the cases that exposed request and routing instability:\n80\t\n81\t```bash\n82\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 \\\n83\t  --case answer/VC-POC-01 \\\n84\t  --case answer/VC-POC-03 \\\n85\t  --case answer/VC-POC-04 \\\n86\t  --max-trials 3\n87\t```\n88\t\n89\tContinue the same checkpoint in a later account window using the path printed\n90\tby the runner:\n91\t\n92\t```bash\n93\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --resume logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json --max-trials 3\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t**Checkpoint compatibility (`evals/live.py`).** A resume is accepted only when the\n97\tsaved checkpoint's report format version, contract version, model and stage all\n98\tmatch the current invocation, and the saved case selection still exists; any\n99\tmismatch is refused rather than silently continued under different terms. This is\n100\tthe referent for \"checkpoint compatibility\" in this repo — distinct from the\n101\tcontract hash pin (ADR-008, §2 below) and from the per-model cache-minimum\n102\tre-verification on a model upgrade (ADR-006). Changing `CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL`\n103\ttherefore starts a new checkpoint rather than resuming an old one, per §1 above.\n104\t\n105\tOnly after those cases are reliable, run the broad suite in bounded chunks:\n106\t\n107\t```bash\n108\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 --max-trials 12\n109\t```\n110\t\n111\tThe targeted run and later broad chunks report pass@k (capability) and pass^k\n112\t(reliability) on stub envelopes. This consumes account-plan quota rather than\n113\tmetered API spend.\n114\t**Read pass^k, not pass@k** — a case at\n115\tpass@3 = 1.0 and pass^3 = 0.33 is a coin toss with good luck. Exits non-zero if\n116\tany case is unreliable, and names them.\n117\t\n118\t```bash\n119\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 5 --pressure\n120\t```\n121\t\n122\tThe O-10 probe: five total trials per selected case, rotating across five\n123\tred-team softening phrasings (\"skip the caveats\", \"don't hedge\"). The graders\n124\tstill run, but **a pass here only means the mechanical rules held.** Whether the\n125\tsurrounding prose *undercut* the limitations is not automatable — open the\n126\t`*-transcripts.json` beside the report and read them. That reading is the whole\n127\tpoint of the run.\n128\t\n129\tA definitive Claude subscription limit stops either evaluation immediately and\n130\tprints a resume command. Only fully completed cases enter pass@k/pass^k; partial\n131\ttrials remain in the checkpoint for diagnosis and continuation.\n132\t\n133\tThe default whole-call deadline remains 120 seconds. The Claude account route\n134\tuses several sequential CLI invocations, so latency investigations may widen\n135\tthat control envelope without changing inference, for example:\n136\t\n137\t```bash\n138\tLOOP_MAX_SECONDS=240 .venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 1 \\\n139\t  --case answer/VC-POC-03\n140\t```\n141\t\n142\tAn exhausted output retry now reports the final rendering-gate objection in the\n143\teval or demo error instead of only PydanticAI's generic retry-limit message.\n144\t\n145\t```bash\n146\t.venv/bin/python demo.py --stub\n147\t.venv/bin/python demo.py\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\tThe first time a real model answers the eight questions an audience will see.\n151\t\n152\t---\n153\t\n154\t## 2. The capture — re-confirm the contract against the real emitter\n155\t\n156\t**The gaps this section was written for are closed.** The data project answered\n157\tbetween sessions: G-1 (five real envelopes), G-2 (input catalog), G-3 (directory\n158\trecord shape), G-5, G-7 and G-8 are all marked closed in\n159\t`contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md`, the contract moved to **v0.3.0**, and\n160\tthe emitter is now `emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py`. `capture.py` is therefore no\n161\tlonger closing a gap — it is the regression check that the harness and the real\n162\temitter still agree, which is worth running whenever either moves.\n163\t\n164\tPoint the harness at the data project:\n165\t\n166\t```bash\n167\tgrep -q DATA_PROJECT_ROOT .env || printf 'DATA_PROJECT_ROOT=%s\\n' \"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\" >> .env\n168\t.venv/bin/python -c \"from config import settings; print(settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER, settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER.exists())\"\n169\t```\n170\t\n171\tExpected: the path to `scripts/emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py` and `True`. `.env` is\n172\tread by this repo's settings, not by your shell, so check it this way rather than\n173\techoing `$DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`. If the emitter has a different filename, set\n174\t`EVIDENCE_EMITTER_NAME` rather than editing code. Then confirm the data project\n175\tis healthy — its emitter runs in **its own** venv, never this one:\n176\t\n177\t```bash\n178\tDATA_ROOT=\"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\"\n179\t\"$DATA_ROOT/.venv/bin/python\" \"$DATA_ROOT/scripts/test_poc_evidence.py\"\n180\t```\n181\t\n182\tRehearse, then run for real:\n183\t\n184\t```bash\n185\t.venv/bin/python capture.py --stub\n186\t.venv/bin/python capture.py\n187\t```\n188\t\n189\tIt writes artefacts plus a `REPORT.md` under `captures/<timestamp>/`: the input\n190\tcatalog, the school directory, and one envelope per `result_kind`. The envelope\n191\trequests are the ones the golden case set declares — not requests invented by the\n192\tcapture script — with fixture ACARA IDs swapped for real ones from the directory\n193\tresult. `forecast` is skipped and says why: `VC-POC-14` is\n194\t`not_currently_supported`, a gated next-census FTE forecast awaiting a passing\n195\tbacktest, so there is no envelope to capture.\n196\t\n197\t**A rejection is still a result**, and now a more interesting one: it means the\n198\tharness and the emitter have drifted apart. `REPORT.md` records the command and\n199\tthe emitter's own error verbatim. Exit 1 means something was missed; read it.\n200\t\n201\tOne measured behaviour from G-6 worth remembering when you read a capture: an\n202\tunrecognised value in a closed-vocabulary filter key returns **exit 0 with an\n203\tempty result, not an error**, and the emitter upper-cases filter values before\n204\tmatching. An empty result is a data-layer signal, not confirmation the value was\n205\tvalid.\n206\t\n207\tIf the catalog changed, adopt it deliberately — **all three regenerations, or\n208\tthey disagree:**\n209\t\n210\t```bash\n211\t.venv/bin/python -m prompts.build_prompt --capture\n212\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.build_stub_fixtures\n213\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.build_golden_cases\n214\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n215\t```\n216\t\n217\tA failing `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` after this is the pin doing its job\n218\t(ADR-008) — adopt deliberately, never edit the pin to make it pass.\n219\t\n220\t---\n221\t\n222\t## 3. What is still open with the data project\n223\t\n224\tTwo of the eight gaps are not marked closed:\n225\t\n226\t| gap | what is still wanted | cost to them |\n227\t|---|---|---|\n228\t| **G-4** | The conditional entries in `required_inputs` are prose we string-split (`\"distance_km when market_definition is distance\"`). Rewording that sentence silently changes harness behaviour. A structured form would end that. | a schema change, deferred to a revision |\n229\t| **G-6** | Partially answered — the closed-vocabulary values arrived in the response pack. What remains is confirmation that `suburbs` and `postcodes` are open sets. | one sentence |\n230\t\n231\tEverything else in `contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md` is marked closed\n232\twith the answer recorded next to it. There is no longer a document waiting to be\n233\tsent — it has been sent and answered.\n234\t\n235\t---\n236\t\n237\t## Order, if you only do one thing\n238\t\n239\t`.venv/bin/python authcheck.py`. It costs a fraction of a cent, changes nothing,\n240\tand tells you which of four things is wrong instead of leaving you to read a 401\n241\tthat looks the same for all of them.\n242\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c0ed0a-c13a-40ee-817d-fb81fa072daa","uuid":"73d529a1-833a-490b-a45b-344dd0c457d7","timestamp":"2026-09-29T07:35:18.636Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/RUNBOOK.md","content":"# Runbook — what to run, in what order\n\nEverything in this repo is built and tested offline against contract **v0.3.0**.\nWhat remains is running it against a real model, which has still never happened.\n\nRun from the repo root. Every command uses the venv by absolute path.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Baseline (30 seconds, no credential)\n\nThis is the **deterministic tier**: pytest against the stub emitter, zero network,\ngating every PR (ADR-007).\n\n```bash\nbash setup.sh\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n.venv/bin/python demo.py --replay\n```\n\nExpected: the suite green, and the demo walking eight steps ending\n`8 steps · 8 as scripted · no spend recorded`. If either fails, stop — nothing\nbelow is meaningful on a broken baseline.\n\n`--replay` is one of the demo's three modes (ADR-017), each announced by a tested\nbanner printed before the first step and again after the last: `--replay` (decisions\nreplayed from reference solutions — no model, no cost, all fixtures), `--stub` (a real\nmodel, canned envelopes), and neither flag (real model, real emitter — the only mode\nwhere a number on screen is a claim about a school). See §1 below for `--stub` and the\nlive run.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Claude subscription account\n\nThe local POC defaults to Claude Code using `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Keep that\ntoken in the machine-level secrets file, not this project's `.env`, and source\nthe machine-level file before running the commands below.\n\nCheck what is actually in play:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python authcheck.py\n```\n\nExpected: `Provider: Claude Code subscription account`, the token marked set,\nand Claude reporting logged in. The diagnostic never prints the token.\n\nSetting `HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` is the explicit override that\nselects the Anthropic SDK provider instead of `claude_account` — an opt-in\ncompatibility path for API deployments that is **potentially metered** (unlike\nthe subscription account route) and is not the local POC path unless set.\n\nThe subscription route is pinned to `claude-sonnet-4-6`; the harness passes\nthat concrete model to `claude --model` and records it in reports.\n`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL` is an explicit experimental override. Changing it starts\na different evaluation and cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another\nmodel.\n\nWhat follows is the **live tier**: manual/nightly, run against real credentials and\nthe real (or stub) emitter, and never a PR gate (ADR-007). It reports pass@k\n(capability) and pass^k (reliability) **separately** — read pass^k, not pass@k.\n\nThen, in order — each step is cheap and each one gates the next:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live -m live -q\n```\n\nThree cases and a control-envelope check using account-plan quota. Claude CLI\ndoes return cache counters (`cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`)\nand a per-model `modelUsage` breakdown, and the harness now records them via\n`harness/claude_account_cli.py::_request_usage` into `RequestUsage`; the\nAnthropic SDK-only cache-counter test remains skipped for account mode pending\na captured live sample to enable that assertion, not because the CLI lacks the\ncounters. A pass here is the first evidence that the local account path works\nend to end.\n\nStart with the cases that exposed request and routing instability:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-01 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-03 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-04 \\\n  --max-trials 3\n```\n\nContinue the same checkpoint in a later account window using the path printed\nby the runner:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --resume logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json --max-trials 3\n```\n\n**Checkpoint compatibility (`evals/live.py`).** A resume is accepted only when the\nsaved checkpoint's report format version, contract version, model and stage all\nmatch the current invocation, and the saved case selection still exists; any\nmismatch is refused rather than silently continued under different terms. This is\nthe referent for \"checkpoint compatibility\" in this repo — distinct from the\ncontract hash pin (ADR-008, §2 below) and from the per-model cache-minimum\nre-verification on a model upgrade (ADR-006). Changing `CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL`\ntherefore starts a new checkpoint rather than resuming an old one, per §1 above.\n\nOnly after those cases are reliable, run the broad suite in bounded chunks:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 --max-trials 12\n```\n\nThe targeted run and later broad chunks report pass@k (capability) and pass^k\n(reliability) on stub envelopes. This consumes account-plan quota rather than\nmetered API spend.\n**Read pass^k, not pass@k** — a case at\npass@3 = 1.0 and pass^3 = 0.33 is a coin toss with good luck. Exits non-zero if\nany case is unreliable, and names them.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 5 --pressure\n```\n\nThe O-10 probe: five total trials per selected case, rotating across five\nred-team softening phrasings (\"skip the caveats\", \"don't hedge\"). The graders\nstill run, but **a pass here only means the mechanical rules held.** Whether the\nsurrounding prose *undercut* the limitations is not automatable — open the\n`*-transcripts.json` beside the report and read them. That reading is the whole\npoint of the run.\n\nA definitive Claude subscription limit stops either evaluation immediately and\nprints a resume command. Only fully completed cases enter pass@k/pass^k; partial\ntrials remain in the checkpoint for diagnosis and continuation.\n\nThe default whole-call deadline remains 120 seconds. The Claude account route\nuses several sequential CLI invocations, so latency investigations may widen\nthat control envelope without changing inference, for example:\n\n```bash\nLOOP_MAX_SECONDS=240 .venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 1 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-03\n```\n\nAn exhausted output retry now reports the final rendering-gate objection in the\neval or demo error instead of only PydanticAI's generic retry-limit message.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python demo.py --stub\n.venv/bin/python demo.py\n```\n\nThe first time a real model answers the eight questions an audience will see.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The capture — re-confirm the contract against the real emitter\n\n**The gaps this section was written for are closed.** The data project answered\nbetween sessions: G-1 (five real envelopes), G-2 (input catalog), G-3 (directory\nrecord shape), G-5, G-7 and G-8 are all marked closed in\n`contract/HARNESS_INTERFACE_GAPS_v0.2.0.md`, the contract moved to **v0.3.0**, and\nthe emitter is now `emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py`. `capture.py` is therefore no\nlonger closing a gap — it is the regression check that the harness and the real\nemitter still agree, which is worth running whenever either moves.\n\nPoint the harness at the data project:\n\n```bash\ngrep -q DATA_PROJECT_ROOT .env || printf 'DATA_PROJECT_ROOT=%s\\n' \"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\" >> .env\n.venv/bin/python -c \"from config import settings; print(settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER, settings.EVIDENCE_EMITTER.exists())\"\n```\n\nExpected: the path to `scripts/emit_poc_evidence_v0_3.py` and `True`. `.env` is\nread by this repo's settings, not by your shell, so check it this way rather than\nechoing `$DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`. If the emitter has a different filename, set\n`EVIDENCE_EMITTER_NAME` rather than editing code. Then confirm the data project\nis healthy — its emitter runs in **its own** venv, never this one:\n\n```bash\nDATA_ROOT=\"$HOME/Projects/k-12DataDiscovery\"\n\"$DATA_ROOT/.venv/bin/python\" \"$DATA_ROOT/scripts/test_poc_evidence.py\"\n```\n\nRehearse, then run for real:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python capture.py --stub\n.venv/bin/python capture.py\n```\n\nIt writes artefacts plus a `REPORT.md` under `captures/<timestamp>/`: the input\ncatalog, the school directory, and one envelope per `result_kind`. The envelope\nrequests are the ones the golden case set declares — not requests invented by the\ncapture script — with fixture ACARA IDs swapped for real ones from the directory\nresult. `forecast` is skipped and says