{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W85uViuwScw3LWmqjdvZEe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# K-12 Market Intelligence — Harness\n2\t\n3\tA natural-language harness over the deterministic evidence contract published by the\n4\tK-12 data project. A PydanticAI agent maps a user's question to an approved question ID\n5\twith a validated structured request, invokes the data layer's emitter, and renders the\n6\treturned evidence envelope faithfully — confidence, provenance and limitations included,\n7\trefusals generated from the contract's own exclusion lists.\n8\t\n9\tThe harness never composes SQL, never touches a database, and never computes a figure.\n10\t\n11\t## Start here\n12\t\n13\t| Read | For |\n14\t|---|---|\n15\t| [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) | The system design — boundary, tools, output contract, eval design, build order |\n16\t| [`docs/decisions.md`](docs/decisions.md) | The ADR log — **source of truth on any conflict** |\n17\t| [`docs/prd.md`](docs/prd.md) + [`docs/prd-addendum.md`](docs/prd-addendum.md) | Product definition (carried verbatim from the planning phase) |\n18\t| [`contract/`](contract/) | The pinned data-layer interface (registry, schemas, handoff, our change requests) |\n19\t| [`HANDOVER.md`](HANDOVER.md) | What is built vs what the next session builds, in order |\n20\t\n21\t## Run\n22\t\n23\t```bash\n24\tbash setup.sh                       # provision .venv from requirements.txt (idempotent)\n25\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q   # unit tier: zero network, runs on every PR\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\tConfiguration lives in `config/settings.py` — the single source of truth for model IDs,\n29\tbudgets, cache minimums, and the data-project location (`DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`). The\n30\t**default provider is `claude_account`** (ADR-019): the Claude CLI under subscription\n31\tOAuth, invoked via `claude --print` with `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` inherited from the\n32\tmachine-level environment — the token is never copied into this project's `.env` — and\n33\tpinned to model `claude-sonnet-4-6` (`config/settings.py` is the single source of truth\n34\tfor that pin; it is not restated here as a literal that can drift). `anthropic_sdk` is\n35\tan explicit, potentially metered opt-in, selected only with\n36\t`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`; it is never the default. See `.env.example` and\n37\t`RUNBOOK.md`.\n38\t\n39\t## Pipeline status (M1–M5)\n40\t\n41\tThe build order in `docs/architecture.md` §12 is complete end to end for the CLI/eval\n42\tPOC: contract pin + stub emitter (M1), golden cases graded before the agent existed\n43\t(M2), the three tools/output union/rendering gate (M3), the frozen prompt and live eval\n44\ttier (M4), and the walked demo across its three modes (M5). Two things are carried but\n45\tintentionally **not** part of that MVP surface:\n46\t\n47\t- **The server layer is unwired (O-2).** A FastAPI scaffold lives under `server/`, but\n48\t  the product surface is CLI + evals; it is wired only when a demo needs a UI.\n49\t- **Forecasting is registered but gated (O-4, `VC-POC-14`).** One next-census School FTE\n50\t  forecast question is registered and `not_currently_supported` until it earns a passing\n51\t  local backtest; it is not part of MVP and a failed/blocked gate is a successful\n52\t  validation outcome, not a defect.\n53\t\n54\t## Live-eval checkpoints\n55\t\n56\t`python -m evals.live` writes a resumable checkpoint (`logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json`)\n57\tafter each trial. A saved checkpoint may be **resumed only when its report format\n58\tversion, its contract version, its model and its stage all match the current run, and\n59\tthe saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh\n60\trun rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the\n61\tcontract hash pin (ADR-008) and the SDK+framework pin (ADR-015-3) — see `RUNBOOK.md` §1.\n62\t\n63\t## Versioning\n64\t\n65\t`VERSION` is bumped by CI at merge — PRs never touch it. Each PR adds one\n66\t`releases/_next/<slug>.md` (copy `releases/_template.md`); the contract is in\n67\t`releases/README.md`.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c0ed0a-c13a-40ee-817d-fb81fa072daa","uuid":"44eb0431-16af-4180-8ca3-6b5975ad69f3","timestamp":"2026-09-29T07:35:21.179Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/README.md","content":"# K-12 Market Intelligence — Harness\n\nA natural-language harness over the deterministic evidence contract published by the\nK-12 data project. A PydanticAI agent maps a user's question to an approved question ID\nwith a validated structured request, invokes the data layer's emitter, and renders the\nreturned evidence envelope faithfully — confidence, provenance and limitations included,\nrefusals generated from the contract's own exclusion lists.\n\nThe harness never composes SQL, never touches a database, and never computes a figure.\n\n## Start here\n\n| Read | For |\n|---|---|\n| [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) | The system design — boundary, tools, output contract, eval design, build order |\n| [`docs/decisions.md`](docs/decisions.md) | The ADR log — **source of truth on any conflict** |\n| [`docs/prd.md`](docs/prd.md) + [`docs/prd-addendum.md`](docs/prd-addendum.md) | Product definition (carried verbatim from the planning phase) |\n| [`contract/`](contract/) | The pinned data-layer interface (registry, schemas, handoff, our change requests) |\n| [`HANDOVER.md`](HANDOVER.md) | What is built vs what the next session builds, in order |\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\nbash setup.sh                       # provision .venv from requirements.txt (idempotent)\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q   # unit tier: zero network, runs on every PR\n```\n\nConfiguration lives in `config/settings.py` — the single source of truth for model IDs,\nbudgets, cache minimums, and the data-project location (`DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`). The\n**default provider is `claude_account`** (ADR-019): the Claude CLI under subscription\nOAuth, invoked via `claude --print` with `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` inherited from the\nmachine-level environment — the token is never copied into this project's `.env` — and\npinned to model `claude-sonnet-4-6` (`config/settings.py` is the single source of truth\nfor that pin; it is not restated here as a literal that can drift). `anthropic_sdk` is\nan explicit, potentially metered opt-in, selected only with\n`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`; it is never the default. See `.env.example` and\n`RUNBOOK.md`.\n\n## Pipeline status (M1–M5)\n\nThe build order in `docs/architecture.md` §12 is complete end to end for the CLI/eval\nPOC: contract pin + stub emitter (M1), golden cases graded before the agent existed\n(M2), the three tools/output union/rendering gate (M3), the frozen prompt and live eval\ntier (M4), and the walked demo across its three modes (M5). Two things are carried but\nintentionally **not** part of that MVP surface:\n\n- **The server layer is unwired (O-2).** A FastAPI scaffold lives under `server/`, but\n  the product surface is CLI + evals; it is wired only when a demo needs a UI.\n- **Forecasting is registered but gated (O-4, `VC-POC-14`).** One next-census School FTE\n  forecast question is registered and `not_currently_supported` until it earns a passing\n  local backtest; it is not part of MVP and a failed/blocked gate is a successful\n  validation outcome, not a defect.\n\n## Live-eval checkpoints\n\n`python -m evals.live` writes a resumable checkpoint (`logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json`)\nafter each trial. A saved checkpoint may be **resumed only when its report format\nversion, its contract version, its model and its stage all match the current run, and\nthe saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh\nrun rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the\ncontract hash pin (ADR-008) and the SDK+framework pin (ADR-015-3) — see `RUNBOOK.md` §1.\n\n## Versioning\n\n`VERSION` is bumped by CI at merge — PRs never touch it. Each PR adds one\n`releases/_next/<slug>.md` (copy `releases/_template.md`); the contract is in\n`releases/README.md`.\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}}}
