{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfXLzGsXSWqG8raCFyNtK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHDaFkzAF87Xekxk2trbLP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md","content":"# vNEXT — Reconcile README/RUNBOOK with implemented pipeline, providers and checkpoints\n\n<!-- Copy to releases/_next/<slug>.md. Do NOT pick a version number and do NOT\n     touch VERSION — release.yml assigns the number at merge and replaces\n     \"vNEXT\" in the heading. Keep \"vNEXT\" literally as written. -->\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-29\n**PR:** #N\n**Type:** patch\n\n<!-- Type must be exactly one of: patch | minor | major (CI enforces this).\n     It drives the version bump at merge. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nREADME.md and RUNBOOK.md are reconciled to the implemented reality: `claude_account`\n(Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) is documented as the default\nprovider per ADR-019, with `anthropic_sdk` as an explicit, potentially metered opt-in.\nThe docs now state the M1–M5 pipeline status honestly (server layer unwired per O-2,\nforecasting registered-but-gated per O-4), name the deterministic and live eval tiers,\nthe `--pressure` probe, the three demo modes, and the live-eval resume/checkpoint\ncompatibility rules implemented in `evals/live.py`. No runtime behaviour changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- README.md: states `claude_account`/`claude-sonnet-4-6` as the ADR-019 default and\n  `anthropic_sdk` as explicit/metered opt-in; adds an honest M1–M5 pipeline status\n  section (server unwired O-2, forecasting gated O-4); documents the live-eval\n  checkpoint compatibility rules from `evals/live.py`.\n- RUNBOOK.md: names the deterministic PR-gate tier (pytest, zero network) and the\n  manual/nightly live tier (pass@k / pass^k reported separately) explicitly; clarifies\n  the `HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` override; documents the three demo modes\n  and banner semantics; states the checkpoint resume compatibility rule (report format\n  version, contract version, model and stage must match, and the saved case selection\n  must still exist).\n- releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md: this note.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py -q\n```\n\nExpected: both commands exit 0 with no failures or errors — this is a docs-only\nchange, so the full suite (including `tests/unit/test_run_cli.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_demo.py` and `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py`) stays green because\n`run.py`, `demo.py` and the contract pin were not touched.\n\n## Rollback\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main -- README.md RUNBOOK.md\ngit rm releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1862,"cache_read_input_tokens":61332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1862},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c0ed0a-c13a-40ee-817d-fb81fa072daa","uuid":"695cedeb-c5d5-4277-b55b-9b07703a8b80","timestamp":"2026-09-29T07:35:31.019Z","request_id":"req_011CfXLzGVwhMAAbK85uFxRG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GHDaFkzAF87Xekxk2trbLP":{"file_path":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md","content":"# vNEXT — Reconcile README/RUNBOOK with implemented pipeline, providers and checkpoints\n\n<!-- Copy to releases/_next/<slug>.md. Do NOT pick a version number and do NOT\n     touch VERSION — release.yml assigns the number at merge and replaces\n     \"vNEXT\" in the heading. Keep \"vNEXT\" literally as written. -->\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-29\n**PR:** #N\n**Type:** patch\n\n<!-- Type must be exactly one of: patch | minor | major (CI enforces this).\n     It drives the version bump at merge. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nREADME.md and RUNBOOK.md are reconciled to the implemented reality: `claude_account`\n(Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) is documented as the default\nprovider per ADR-019, with `anthropic_sdk` as an explicit, potentially metered opt-in.\nThe docs now state the M1–M5 pipeline status honestly (server layer unwired per O-2,\nforecasting registered-but-gated per O-4), name the deterministic and live eval tiers,\nthe `--pressure` probe, the three demo modes, and the live-eval resume/checkpoint\ncompatibility rules implemented in `evals/live.py`. No runtime behaviour changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- README.md: states `claude_account`/`claude-sonnet-4-6` as the ADR-019 default and\n  `anthropic_sdk` as explicit/metered opt-in; adds an honest M1–M5 pipeline status\n  section (server unwired O-2, forecasting gated O-4); documents the live-eval\n  checkpoint compatibility rules from `evals/live.py`.\n- RUNBOOK.md: names the deterministic PR-gate tier (pytest, zero network) and the\n  manual/nightly live tier (pass@k / pass^k reported separately) explicitly; clarifies\n  the `HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` override; documents the three demo modes\n  and banner semantics; states the checkpoint resume compatibility rule (report format\n  version, contract version, model and stage must match, and the saved case selection\n  must still exist).\n- releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md: this note.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py -q\n```\n\nExpected: both commands exit 0 with no failures or errors — this is a docs-only\nchange, so the full suite (including `tests/unit/test_run_cli.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_demo.py` and `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py`) stays green because\n`run.py`, `demo.py` and the contract pin were not touched.\n\n## Rollback\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main -- README.md RUNBOOK.md\ngit rm releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md\n```\n"}}}
